course: dictionary
lesson: 6335
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. «Mount» is one of them, so you cannot know its meaning from the word alone. The words around it are its context, and they tell you which meaning is right.
explain: «The knight mounted his horse and rode off.» Mounted means got on, because you get on a horse before you ride it. «Worries mounted as the storm came closer.» Here mounted means grew bigger and bigger, because worries cannot be ridden.
explain: Mount is also part of a name, like «Mount Everest». There it is not an action at all: it tells you the name belongs to a mountain. Ask yourself: which meaning fits the sentence? Then try it in place of the word and see if it still makes sense.
fact: «Mount» can be a verb (mount, mounts, mounted, mounting) or a noun (a mount, mounts).
fact: To mount means to get on a horse or bike, or to go up or climb, or to slowly increase, as in «worries mounted».
fact: To mount something means to fix it onto a wall or stand, or onto card for display.
fact: «Mount Everest, on the border of Nepal and China, is the highest mountain above sea level at 8,849 metres.»
fact: A mount is a horse for riding, or a stand or card that holds something.
exercise: «The knight mounted his horse and rode off.» What does mounted mean here? | Hid | Fell off | Washed | *Got on
exercise: «Worries mounted as the storm came closer.» What does mounted mean here? | Went to sleep | Got smaller and quieter | Stood still | *Grew bigger and bigger
exercise: Pupils mount their artwork on coloured card for the school display. What does mount mean? | Sell it to a shop | *Fix it onto card to show it | Make it smaller | Throw it away
test: «Mount Everest is the highest mountain above sea level.» In this sentence, what is Mount? | Adverb, a word about how | Verb, an action word | *Part of a name | Adjective, a describing word
test: Which sentence uses mount to mean fix something onto a wall or card? | The worries mounted all night | *Dad will mount the photo on the wall | The horse will mount the hill slowly | The climbers will mount the mountain at dawn
exam: In «with Mount Fuji in the distance», what does Mount tell you? | To climb up it | *It is part of the name of a mountain | To fix it on card | A horse to ride
